            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Foreign Policy in the Middle East</strong><br>\nBush's foreign policy was marked by the promotion of democracy, the \"Bush Doctrine\" of preemptive war, and strained international relations due to his policies in the Middle East.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Post-Presidency</strong><br>\nSince leaving office in 2009, Bush has focused on humanitarian efforts, including work on veteran support and African development, and taken up painting.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Personal Reflections</strong><br>\nBush is noted for his commitment to conservatism, his Texan identity, and having one of the most contentious and eventful presidencies in modern history.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
